Translating a cast through a deep chain of newtypes, such as `((b as Layer0) as Layer1) ... as LayerN`, no longer takes time cubic in the depth of the chain (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/378). The Boogie translator now remembers, for the rest of a module's translation, the ancestor type it computed for each type it converts, in each visibility scope. The emitted Boogie is unchanged.
